-# The DevTools Times
+# smallpt lab
 
-This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
+A browser playground for [Kevin Beason’s smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/), compiled from C++ to WebAssembly with Emscripten. Rendering runs in a dedicated Web Worker; pixels are progressively copied onto a canvas. No render server or cross-origin isolation headers are needed.
 
+## Run
 
 ```sh
-pnpm install && pnpm run start
+pnpm install
+pnpm dev --host 0.0.0.0
 ```
 
-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+The homepage renders the original Cornell box. Randomize colors changes both foreground sphere colors and the wall palette, then starts a new render. You can also edit sphere colors, select quality, reset the scene, or save the current image as a PNG. Starting another render terminates the previous worker.
 
-## Tech Stack
+## Build
 
-- **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
-- **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
-- **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
-- **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+```sh
+pnpm build
+pnpm start
+```
+
+The homepage is prerendered to `dist/client/index.html`. Compiled WebAssembly files are included in `public/wasm`, so the app build does not require Emscripten. Use HTTP to serve the page; module workers cannot run from a `file://` URL.
+
+To rebuild the renderer with Emscripten installed:
+
+```sh
+pnpm build:wasm
+pnpm check:wasm
+```
+
+`native/smallpt-original.cpp` preserves the upstream source. `native/smallpt.cpp` keeps its integrator and adds an incremental RGBA output interface and sphere color setters. The MIT license is in `native/LICENSE.smallpt`. The browser port uses one worker instead of OpenMP.
+
+The included preview is real output from the compiled WebAssembly renderer, generated at 640 × 480 and 512 samples per pixel. Regenerate it without a browser:
+
+```sh
+node scripts/check-renderer.mjs --preview
+```
+
+This script also checks illuminated RGBA output, deterministic reset, the effect of changing sphere colors, and progressive sampling. Browser verification was intentionally omitted.
